WEBVTT

00:00:01.680 --> 00:00:05.230
Satoshi, who aims to battle
the Supreme Monarch, Dande...

00:00:05.650 --> 00:00:10.240
And Go, who dreams of catching every Pokémon
to work his way up to Mew...

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:15.530
This is the story of
their lives and adventures.

00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:21.750
This is Kuchiba City.

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:25.210
It looks like Koharu and Eevee
are on their way back from school.

00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:27.540
Koharu!

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:29.550
Stop that Pokémon!

00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:31.210
Whaa?! Stop it?!

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:37.930
Now, Go!

00:00:37.930 --> 00:00:39.850
Monster Ball, go!

00:00:49.690 --> 00:00:53.570
Biriridama’s data will be
added to the Index!

00:00:53.570 --> 00:00:55.280
All right!

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:57.370
Sheesh...
You really gave me a shock.

00:00:57.370 --> 00:01:01.660
Sorry. I just had to catch
this alternate-color guy!

00:01:02.540 --> 00:01:05.370
Blue Biriridama are pretty rare.

00:01:05.370 --> 00:01:07.380
Ooh, that’s a pretty blue.

00:01:07.380 --> 00:01:08.540
Watch out, though.

00:01:08.540 --> 00:01:10.590
It’ll blow up if you touch it by mistake.

00:01:10.590 --> 00:01:12.880
My, what a lika-blue target!

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:17.140
I’m so excited!
I just can’t contain myself!

00:01:17.140 --> 00:01:18.140
Hold on!

00:01:23.890 --> 00:01:25.770
Oh, sorry...

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:30.360
Your Biriridama was just so beautiful
it pulled me in.

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:31.770
Uh, who are you?

00:01:31.770 --> 00:01:36.030
I’m a Blue Pokémaniac from Kalos...

00:01:36.030 --> 00:01:37.160
Abel.

00:01:37.160 --> 00:01:42.870
I’m visiting Kanto to enjoy this and that,
and everything about blue Pokémon!

00:01:43.330 --> 00:01:44.950
A Blue Pokémaniac?

00:01:44.950 --> 00:01:47.620
Does that mean
you like blue Pokémon?

00:01:47.620 --> 00:01:48.880
Right you are!

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:53.550
Blue is cool and refreshing...
yet it’s also the color of the hottest flames!

00:01:53.550 --> 00:01:58.380
Their protean charms have
grabbed me tight and never let go!

00:01:59.180 --> 00:02:02.640
Futachimaru!
Discipline Pokémon! Water type!

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:09.310
Strict training is how it learns
its flowing double-hotachi technique!

00:02:09.690 --> 00:02:11.770
So that’s why your partner is blue.

00:02:12.320 --> 00:02:17.900
My partner adds so much flavor to my life that I could stomach
ten whole plain baguettes without so much as a gripe!

00:02:19.530 --> 00:02:20.740
What do you say, kids?

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:23.160
Meeting you here must be
the hand of fate at work!

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:25.950
Why not try Aokatsu with me?

00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:27.000
Aokatsu?

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:31.000
katsudou
aoi
Blue Pokémon-related activities,
or Aokatsu for short!

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:33.670
How about some research, then?

00:02:33.670 --> 00:02:34.590
I’m in!

00:02:34.590 --> 00:02:36.590
Um, I’d rather...

00:02:36.590 --> 00:02:37.380
Eevee?

00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:39.590
Well then, off to Aokatsu we...

00:02:39.590 --> 00:02:41.180
...go!

00:02:41.180 --> 00:02:42.850
Whaaat?!

00:04:21.280 --> 00:04:25.570
Doesn’t it feel like
we’ve been stuck in a rut lately?

00:04:25.570 --> 00:04:30.950
We need to enact some huge plan with bombastic results...
something with a <i>bang,</i> a <i>boom!</i>

00:04:30.950 --> 00:04:34.290
That’s great and all,
but we don’t have the funds, meow.

00:04:34.750 --> 00:04:36.960
Huh? Aren’t those the brat boys?

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:38.130
They are, meow.

00:04:38.130 --> 00:04:40.630
Since I came all this way to Kanto,

00:04:40.630 --> 00:04:44.090
I made sure to plan everything out
so I don’t miss anything whatsoever!

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:46.890
Wow, that’s a packed schedule!

00:04:47.350 --> 00:04:50.680
And naturally, I’m starting with
the Blue Poké-Photo Exhibition!

00:04:50.680 --> 00:04:55.770
They have photos featuring blue Pokémon from
all over the world. A must-see for Blue Pokémaniacs!

00:04:55.770 --> 00:04:57.150
Huh...

00:04:57.940 --> 00:04:59.610
Blue Pokémaniacs, he said.

00:04:59.610 --> 00:05:02.990
Guess there’s all sorts of hobbies
out there, meow.

00:05:02.990 --> 00:05:04.780
Isn’t this our chance?

00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:05.660
Meow?

00:05:05.660 --> 00:05:09.780
I mean, maniacs will spend tons
on what they’re into, right?

00:05:09.780 --> 00:05:11.740
So, if we make use of that...

00:05:11.740 --> 00:05:14.160
We’ll be rolling in operation funds!

00:05:15.920 --> 00:05:18.750
I like! I like!
This place is a flood of likes!

00:05:18.750 --> 00:05:23.050
With all this blue calling to me
from every angle, I’ll run out of likes!

00:05:23.050 --> 00:05:25.340
This place really is full of
blue Poké-Photos.

00:05:25.340 --> 00:05:27.510
It’s a little overwhelming...

00:05:30.680 --> 00:05:32.350
Oh, Pikachu!

00:05:37.060 --> 00:05:38.060
We should look, too.

00:05:38.060 --> 00:05:39.060
Yeah.

00:05:39.060 --> 00:05:40.610
Non-non, kids!

00:05:41.070 --> 00:05:43.230
Encounters like these
are once-in-a-lifetime!

00:05:43.230 --> 00:05:45.150
You need to <i>savor</i> them!

00:05:45.150 --> 00:05:46.950
So that’s Aokatsu, huh?

00:05:46.950 --> 00:05:49.030
Uh, “savor them”?

00:05:49.030 --> 00:05:52.330
Admire them and
let your imagination run wild.

00:05:52.830 --> 00:05:54.500
For instance, this Oshamari!

00:05:54.500 --> 00:05:57.120
See how she has a gentle
yet beautiful blue.

00:05:57.120 --> 00:05:59.960
They’re skillful dancers
that love to practice their craft.

00:05:59.960 --> 00:06:02.040
But the eyes are
what draw your attention.

00:06:02.040 --> 00:06:03.840
She looks as though
she’s lost deep in thought...

00:06:04.340 --> 00:06:07.380
Perhaps she’s on a quest...

00:06:07.380 --> 00:06:09.840
A quest to find
the reason why she dances!

00:06:09.840 --> 00:06:13.050
Then one day,
her worries cause an accident...

00:06:15.930 --> 00:06:18.060
Are you okay?

00:06:20.270 --> 00:06:24.280
Of course, being wild,
she’ll be wary around me.

00:06:24.280 --> 00:06:26.690
But I won’t take advantage
of her vulnerability.

00:06:27.530 --> 00:06:31.450
Then some day,
my feelings will truly reach her...

00:06:32.070 --> 00:06:35.240
You’re all better now.
Fare thee well.

00:06:41.830 --> 00:06:43.790
Oshamari!

00:06:43.790 --> 00:06:49.470
I’ll wholeheartedly accept the loving dances
she performs each day for none other than me!

00:06:50.590 --> 00:06:54.140
And that will be the beginning
of a wonderful life together!

00:06:54.140 --> 00:06:55.850
Wh-When did you grab her...?!

00:06:55.850 --> 00:06:58.430
All that from just one photo...

00:06:58.430 --> 00:07:00.650
So those are
the fantasies of a maniac...

00:07:00.650 --> 00:07:01.940
Simpleton!

00:07:01.940 --> 00:07:04.860
Your imagination is far too simple!

00:07:04.860 --> 00:07:06.820
You’re forcing your own desires on her!

00:07:06.820 --> 00:07:09.240
You’ve lost sight of the true Oshamari!

00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:12.870
Wh-What?! Brutus, why are you...?!

00:07:15.080 --> 00:07:16.660
Do they know each other?

00:07:16.660 --> 00:07:19.080
He does have a blue Pokémon...

00:07:19.080 --> 00:07:22.710
Nyaonyx!
Constraint Pokémon! Psychic type!

00:07:22.710 --> 00:07:25.000
The defensive instinct of
the males is strong!

00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:29.630
It’s when they’re protecting themselves or their partners
that they unleash their full power!

00:07:29.630 --> 00:07:31.720
Cease the false allegations!

00:07:31.720 --> 00:07:33.340
But I can tell.

00:07:33.340 --> 00:07:36.760
Those are the eyes of one
wishing to become stronger!

00:07:37.140 --> 00:07:42.730
Perhaps her home was taken over
by some barbaric Pokémon!

00:07:46.480 --> 00:07:47.530
Do not cry.

00:07:47.530 --> 00:07:49.990
Are you really
willing to give up now?

00:07:50.530 --> 00:07:51.530
Follow me!

00:07:51.530 --> 00:07:55.160
Your regrets will drive you
to become stronger!

00:07:57.910 --> 00:08:00.790
Hang in there!
You’ve nearly overcome your limits!

00:08:02.290 --> 00:08:04.290
Aim to be an Ashirène!

00:08:04.630 --> 00:08:07.920
Then, at the end of her harsh training,
Oshamari will...

00:08:10.670 --> 00:08:11.880
You finally did it!

00:08:11.880 --> 00:08:13.460
Hold it right there!

00:08:14.010 --> 00:08:15.800
The blue on her tail is too dark!

00:08:15.800 --> 00:08:18.390
You need a story dyed
in Oshamari Blue!

00:08:18.390 --> 00:08:19.640
Oh, don’t worry.

00:08:19.640 --> 00:08:22.640
There’s still a passionate
Ashirène Blue tale to come.

00:08:22.640 --> 00:08:25.310
Wouldn’t you agree,
Blue Poké-Miss?

00:08:25.310 --> 00:08:27.190
What, me?!

00:08:27.570 --> 00:08:29.900
Because she has blue on her clothes?

00:08:29.900 --> 00:08:30.860
You’ve got it wrong!

00:08:30.860 --> 00:08:32.700
This is my school uniform...

00:08:32.700 --> 00:08:34.160
Attention, please!

00:08:35.950 --> 00:08:40.490
Do we have any guests today
in need of a little extra Poké-Blue?

00:08:40.490 --> 00:08:41.750
Poké-Blue?!

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:46.750
What an amazing glossy luster!

00:08:46.750 --> 00:08:48.750
I’ve never seen a
Sonansu like this before!

00:08:48.750 --> 00:08:52.760
This beauty is one in a hundred—
no, a thousand!

00:08:52.760 --> 00:08:56.590
Why not take a commemorative
photo with our Sonansu?

00:08:57.600 --> 00:08:58.680
Can you send the file?!

00:08:58.680 --> 00:08:59.680
I’ll make it my new wallpaper!

00:08:59.680 --> 00:09:01.850
I’ll put it under my pillow
and have wonderful dreams!

00:09:01.850 --> 00:09:03.680
I’ll talk to it when I’m feeling lonely!

00:09:03.680 --> 00:09:05.560
I’ll print it on a body pillow!

00:09:05.560 --> 00:09:06.560
That’s wonderful.

00:09:06.560 --> 00:09:08.230
All right!

00:09:08.940 --> 00:09:10.150
Hey, where are you going?

00:09:10.150 --> 00:09:11.650
Come back here!

00:09:12.570 --> 00:09:13.690
Oh, dear...

00:09:13.690 --> 00:09:15.950
It’s your fault he ran away!

00:09:15.950 --> 00:09:19.240
You’re the reason
that one-in-a-thousand—

00:09:21.370 --> 00:09:24.080
Such amazing blue!

00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:31.170
Why did I have to run into <i>him?!</i>

00:09:31.170 --> 00:09:33.590
We’ve met a few times before
in offline meetups.

00:09:33.590 --> 00:09:35.590
And if I say right, he’ll say left...

00:09:35.590 --> 00:09:38.140
If I point up, he’ll point down!

00:09:38.140 --> 00:09:40.810
He’s <i>always</i> at my throat!

00:09:40.810 --> 00:09:43.180
I guess maniacs come in all stripes.

00:09:43.180 --> 00:09:45.640
That’s what happens
when they’re both super fixated.

00:09:45.640 --> 00:09:49.060
But! That’s enough
of feeling anxious!

00:09:49.060 --> 00:09:49.650
Huh?

00:09:49.650 --> 00:09:50.610
What do you mean?

00:09:50.610 --> 00:09:53.070
I want to enjoy this trip!

00:09:53.070 --> 00:09:56.070
I’m going to flush that bother
down the toilet!

00:09:56.070 --> 00:09:56.860
The toilet, huh?

00:09:56.860 --> 00:09:57.910
Now, let’s go!

00:09:57.910 --> 00:09:59.910
We have blue excitement in store!

00:09:59.910 --> 00:10:01.660
Enjoy Aokatsu!

00:10:01.660 --> 00:10:03.450
Aokatsu!

00:10:06.080 --> 00:10:08.790
C’mon, you can’t just run for it...

00:10:08.790 --> 00:10:12.090
Yeah. You have the blue
everyone’s looking for.

00:10:14.880 --> 00:10:19.050
Seems like they scared him
like nothing ever has, meow.

00:10:19.050 --> 00:10:21.470
Well, they were really imposing...

00:10:21.470 --> 00:10:24.390
Don’t worry!
They’re not gonna bite.

00:10:24.390 --> 00:10:25.850
So hang in ther— Huh?

00:10:28.520 --> 00:10:29.770
It was <i>that</i> bad?!

00:10:29.770 --> 00:10:31.150
Well, if you <i>really</i> don’t want to...

00:10:31.150 --> 00:10:34.730
...Then we’ll just have to
work something out on our own, meow.

00:10:37.530 --> 00:10:39.530
Pocket Monsters!

00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:50.920
This is our next destination!

00:10:52.420 --> 00:10:54.380
Everything’s all blue...

00:10:54.380 --> 00:10:56.210
Very lika-blue, right?

00:10:56.210 --> 00:10:59.680
The Blue Pokémaniac bartender
is running a collab café!

00:11:02.430 --> 00:11:04.350
These color gradients...!

00:11:04.350 --> 00:11:06.430
I kinda like this uniform look!

00:11:06.430 --> 00:11:08.850
You’re all starting to get it!

00:11:08.850 --> 00:11:10.520
Bartender, bring us those!

00:11:11.730 --> 00:11:13.020
Coming up.

00:11:18.780 --> 00:11:21.070
Blue Juice from the collab menu!

00:11:21.070 --> 00:11:25.160
We can taste blue in a blue space
while observing Poké-Blues!

00:11:25.160 --> 00:11:27.410
This is Aokatsu at its finest!

00:11:33.040 --> 00:11:33.710
Simpleton!

00:11:33.710 --> 00:11:35.790
Once again,
far too simpleminded!

00:11:35.790 --> 00:11:36.800
That voice...

00:11:36.800 --> 00:11:38.300
Oh! You again?!

00:11:38.300 --> 00:11:40.220
We meet again...

00:11:42.010 --> 00:11:45.390
You try so hard to be a maniac,
but you weren’t prepared!

00:11:45.390 --> 00:11:47.350
Whoa, his food is amazing!

00:11:47.350 --> 00:11:50.640
The Fair-exclusive
Crazy Blue Pancakes!

00:11:50.640 --> 00:11:54.690
Dough made from Yache Berries,
and if that wasn’t enough, topped with Oran Cream!

00:11:54.690 --> 00:11:57.690
A dish that every
Blue Pokémaniac should try!

00:11:57.690 --> 00:12:01.650
And for your information, you need to book it
ahead of time, so you can’t order it for today!

00:12:02.030 --> 00:12:05.120
What if I didn’t
<i>because</i> I’m a Blue Pokémaniac?

00:12:05.120 --> 00:12:05.870
What?!

00:12:06.530 --> 00:12:07.790
Thank you for waiting.

00:12:07.790 --> 00:12:08.910
What?!

00:12:08.910 --> 00:12:12.120
The secret menu based on staff meals,
that only true connoisseurs know.

00:12:12.120 --> 00:12:15.920
Soaked in Chiigo and Nekobu juice,
then baked in an oven,

00:12:15.920 --> 00:12:18.420
the sweet-and-sour
Chiigo Nekobu Toast!

00:12:20.260 --> 00:12:21.630
Exquisite!

00:12:21.630 --> 00:12:24.840
The simple but moreish
beloved long-seller!

00:12:24.840 --> 00:12:27.850
<i>This</i> is what a true maniac
would select!

00:12:29.260 --> 00:12:33.640
My pancakes are stuffed with the bartender’s
blue Poké-Love! They’re much better!

00:12:37.690 --> 00:12:39.270
There they go again.

00:12:39.270 --> 00:12:41.320
They should savor their food more.

00:12:41.320 --> 00:12:43.700
Hey, this is pretty tasty.

00:12:44.110 --> 00:12:45.700
How could this happen?!

00:12:45.700 --> 00:12:48.950
I was so excited to eat it,
but I can’t even remember the taste!

00:12:48.950 --> 00:12:50.950
Things did get heated in there...

00:12:50.950 --> 00:12:54.120
I wonder why Brutus
keeps finding you...

00:12:54.120 --> 00:12:55.920
I think I sort of get it.

00:12:56.920 --> 00:13:00.800
Like something enough and you want to prove it,
which just makes you fixate more on it, yeah?

00:13:00.800 --> 00:13:03.670
I’d rather just enjoy it
together, though...

00:13:03.670 --> 00:13:04.680
Me, too.

00:13:04.680 --> 00:13:07.340
Now, next up is a top-choice candy!

00:13:07.340 --> 00:13:08.390
Candy?

00:13:08.390 --> 00:13:11.020
Yes, that’s the next Aokatsu point!

00:13:11.020 --> 00:13:15.230
This is bound to mend
my frayed nerves!

00:13:15.230 --> 00:13:16.150
Here, watch this!

00:13:18.650 --> 00:13:24.650
A cooling Vanipetit from far away
fell in love with a cool Gekogashira.

00:13:24.650 --> 00:13:29.030
Their tale is now available as candy!

00:13:29.030 --> 00:13:32.660
Marine-do’s Marbled Candy,
Super Blue flavor.

00:13:35.460 --> 00:13:39.040
Every Blue Pokémaniac knows
this masterpiece of a commercial!

00:13:39.040 --> 00:13:41.050
And this is where it was filmed!

00:13:41.050 --> 00:13:43.460
We are standing on sacred ground!

00:13:43.460 --> 00:13:45.300
Huh, I never knew.

00:13:45.720 --> 00:13:49.800
The amazing choice of two Poké-Blues as the Marbled Candy mascots!

00:13:49.800 --> 00:13:53.060
This goes beyond lika-blue,
this is the birth of lova-blue!

00:13:53.060 --> 00:13:54.930
Simpleton!

00:13:54.930 --> 00:13:59.560
I didn’t plan to stick my nose in,
but your knowledge is severely lacking.

00:13:59.560 --> 00:14:00.440
Again...?

00:14:00.440 --> 00:14:02.650
But I guess that’s to be expected!

00:14:02.650 --> 00:14:04.860
You’re ridiculing that godly ad?!

00:14:04.860 --> 00:14:06.450
Of course not.

00:14:06.450 --> 00:14:10.070
But there was only <i>one</i> blue Pokémon
in it, the Gekogashira!

00:14:10.070 --> 00:14:13.580
Because Vanipetit is
a white Pokémon!

00:14:13.580 --> 00:14:15.410
What?!

00:14:15.410 --> 00:14:19.670
The shaded parts of Vanipetit may look blue,
but it’s a white Pokémon!

00:14:19.670 --> 00:14:22.840
Classifying it as a blue Pokémon
is a blue-ge mistake!

00:14:22.840 --> 00:14:23.840
Objection!

00:14:23.840 --> 00:14:25.340
There are many
Poké-Blues in the world,

00:14:25.340 --> 00:14:29.220
but is there a single other Pokémon
with blue so pure and clear?!

00:14:32.180 --> 00:14:35.560
Hmm... Is Vanipetit blue,
or is it white...?

00:14:35.560 --> 00:14:37.560
A hard question for sure.

00:14:38.350 --> 00:14:41.190
Oh, we finally found you, guests!

00:14:42.440 --> 00:14:44.440
The Sonansu from earlier!

00:14:46.820 --> 00:14:49.950
...is what it looks like,
but it’s actually me inside, meow!

00:14:51.820 --> 00:14:53.530
It doesn’t thrill me.

00:14:53.530 --> 00:14:55.080
My soul is utterly unmoved.

00:14:55.080 --> 00:14:56.950
They’re suspicious?!

00:14:57.540 --> 00:15:00.210
I’ll just have to appeal
to them with <i>that,</i> meow.

00:15:00.210 --> 00:15:02.710
Sonyansu!

00:15:06.090 --> 00:15:06.670
Oh, dear me!

00:15:06.670 --> 00:15:09.510
My dear Sonansu,
are you not feeling well?

00:15:09.510 --> 00:15:11.680
Excuse us!

00:15:12.930 --> 00:15:14.970
I’ve had enough!

00:15:14.970 --> 00:15:17.810
Why do you always interfere
with my Aokatsu!

00:15:17.810 --> 00:15:21.060
What?! You should stop
following me everywhere!

00:15:21.060 --> 00:15:24.690
Why do those two
keep finding one another?

00:15:25.270 --> 00:15:28.150
Maybe they both
have the same itinerary.

00:15:28.150 --> 00:15:29.400
What do you mean?

00:15:29.400 --> 00:15:30.700
He said it before, remember?

00:15:30.740 --> 00:15:32.820
Since I came all this way to Kanto,

00:15:32.820 --> 00:15:36.080
I made sure to plan everything out
so I don’t miss anything whatsoever!

00:15:36.490 --> 00:15:37.830
I get it.

00:15:37.830 --> 00:15:39.540
Since they’re both
Blue Pokémaniacs,

00:15:39.540 --> 00:15:43.250
if they focus on efficiency,
they could end up with identical plans.

00:15:43.250 --> 00:15:44.750
No way!

00:15:46.000 --> 00:15:46.920
What’s that?

00:15:49.170 --> 00:15:52.680
Marine-do’s Marbled Candy,
Super Blue flavor.

00:15:52.680 --> 00:15:56.930
Get the commemorative
5th anniversary plush.

00:15:56.930 --> 00:15:58.350
You, too?!

00:15:58.350 --> 00:15:59.730
In this city,
this sacred ground?!

00:15:59.730 --> 00:16:01.810
You planned on getting it?!

00:16:06.820 --> 00:16:08.150
Where are they going?

00:16:08.150 --> 00:16:10.530
Looks like Koharu
had the right idea.

00:16:10.530 --> 00:16:11.320
Let’s go!

00:16:11.320 --> 00:16:12.740
Right!

00:16:13.240 --> 00:16:15.530
Please stop, customers!

00:16:15.530 --> 00:16:16.240
Is this it?

00:16:16.240 --> 00:16:17.540
Let go!

00:16:17.540 --> 00:16:20.620
Um... We only have one plushie
in today’s stock...

00:16:20.620 --> 00:16:22.410
They’re really fighting over it.

00:16:22.410 --> 00:16:24.040
I’ll take you home!

00:16:24.040 --> 00:16:25.330
They want to come with me!

00:16:25.960 --> 00:16:28.050
If you keep pulling...

00:16:30.630 --> 00:16:32.260
Oh, dear...

00:16:32.260 --> 00:16:34.470
Ripping the lovers apart...

00:16:34.470 --> 00:16:36.640
...how could you be so cruel?!

00:16:38.260 --> 00:16:41.310
They <i>really</i> don’t get along,
do they...?

00:16:41.310 --> 00:16:44.560
From another point of view,
maybe they’re perfect for each other?

00:16:44.560 --> 00:16:46.440
Who knows anymore?

00:16:46.810 --> 00:16:48.650
But now they’ve crossed a line...

00:16:48.650 --> 00:16:50.030
I’ve made up my mind!

00:16:50.030 --> 00:16:52.110
I challenge you to a battle!

00:16:52.110 --> 00:16:53.400
My pleasure.

00:16:54.860 --> 00:16:57.120
...I guess they’re
going to go all the way.

00:16:57.120 --> 00:16:57.990
Yeah.

00:17:00.240 --> 00:17:01.830
You know the rules, right?

00:17:01.830 --> 00:17:05.290
The loser immediately stops their Aokatsu
and goes back to Kalos.

00:17:05.290 --> 00:17:07.500
They don’t have to go that far...

00:17:07.500 --> 00:17:09.750
I think this could be interesting!

00:17:09.750 --> 00:17:12.300
Yeah, it’s a serious battle
between two maniacs!

00:17:12.760 --> 00:17:13.420
Hmm?

00:17:17.340 --> 00:17:19.430
Time for a Poké-Blue battle!

00:17:19.430 --> 00:17:20.560
Let’s go!

00:17:27.230 --> 00:17:29.230
A double battle?!

00:17:50.170 --> 00:17:52.250
What are they doing?

00:17:53.210 --> 00:17:55.300
Maybe it’s a “Blue Poké-Test”?

00:17:55.300 --> 00:17:56.550
What’s that?

00:17:56.550 --> 00:18:00.010
You know, like blind taste tests
where people guess the food.

00:18:00.010 --> 00:18:00.930
It couldn’t be...

00:18:01.390 --> 00:18:02.810
You’d never guess something like...

00:18:02.810 --> 00:18:04.810
The sky blue Nidorina!

00:18:04.810 --> 00:18:06.560
The horizon blue Gomazo!

00:18:07.560 --> 00:18:09.520
The aquamarine Gamageroge!

00:18:09.520 --> 00:18:11.230
The ultramarine Gureggru!

00:18:11.230 --> 00:18:12.730
They got it right!

00:18:12.730 --> 00:18:13.570
Awesome!

00:18:13.570 --> 00:18:14.940
They really are maniacs!

00:18:14.940 --> 00:18:16.570
You’re not half bad.

00:18:16.570 --> 00:18:19.490
You aren’t either. But these won’t...

00:18:22.700 --> 00:18:24.080
Sarunori!
Eevee!

00:18:24.080 --> 00:18:24.950
What’s going on?!

00:18:25.580 --> 00:18:29.330
If you say
“Eevee! Sarunori! What’s going on?!”...

00:18:29.790 --> 00:18:32.420
We’ll answer out of
sympathy for the world!

00:18:33.800 --> 00:18:36.300
To protect the world from devastation.

00:18:36.300 --> 00:18:39.260
To preserve world peace.

00:18:39.260 --> 00:18:42.680
Championing the evils
of truth and love.

00:18:42.680 --> 00:18:45.470
We’re the lovely, charming villains.

00:18:45.930 --> 00:18:46.680
Musashi!

00:18:46.680 --> 00:18:47.930
Kojiro!

00:18:47.930 --> 00:18:51.560
The Team Rocket duo
soars through the galaxy!

00:18:51.560 --> 00:18:54.690
Like a white hole,
a white tomorrow awaits us!

00:18:54.690 --> 00:18:57.190
Just kidding, meow!

00:19:01.370 --> 00:19:03.830
Sonansu!

00:19:04.370 --> 00:19:06.660
Without Sonansu...

00:19:06.660 --> 00:19:08.250
...the motto just fizzles out, meow...

00:19:08.250 --> 00:19:09.830
This is all your fault!

00:19:09.830 --> 00:19:11.170
What?!

00:19:11.170 --> 00:19:12.710
Who are you?!

00:19:12.710 --> 00:19:15.210
They’re bad guys
who steal people’s Pokémon!

00:19:15.210 --> 00:19:16.090
What?!

00:19:16.090 --> 00:19:20.260
This time, we decided
to go back to basics, meow.

00:19:20.260 --> 00:19:24.510
The brat boy’s Pikachu,
and the maniacs’ spectacular Poké-Blues...

00:19:24.510 --> 00:19:26.720
If we present them all
to Sakaki as a set...

00:19:26.720 --> 00:19:29.480
He’ll give us a raise for sure.

00:19:29.480 --> 00:19:31.060
Kojiro, get ‘em!

00:19:31.060 --> 00:19:31.850
Roger!

00:19:32.480 --> 00:19:33.730
We’ll catch them all with one net!

00:19:33.730 --> 00:19:35.940
Nyaonyx! Charm Voice!

00:19:39.320 --> 00:19:41.410
Futachimaru, save Pikachu
and the others!

00:19:48.910 --> 00:19:49.710
Ow!

00:19:50.660 --> 00:19:52.420
Thanks, Futachimaru!

00:19:52.420 --> 00:19:56.290
Nyaonyx, drag them down
with psycho power!

00:20:05.720 --> 00:20:08.640
How dare you try to
lay a hand on our Poké-Blues?!

00:20:08.640 --> 00:20:11.310
Your crimes are far too grave!

00:20:13.350 --> 00:20:16.400
They were fighting until a moment ago...

00:20:16.400 --> 00:20:18.440
This could be good!

00:20:19.400 --> 00:20:21.860
Then we’ll have to take them
by force, meow!

00:20:21.860 --> 00:20:24.070
Vending, come on!

00:20:26.410 --> 00:20:28.910
It’s so lika-blue!

00:20:28.910 --> 00:20:31.710
Pelipper, darling!
Come this way! Come here!

00:20:31.710 --> 00:20:33.790
Come on down!

00:20:39.170 --> 00:20:41.550
You’re running away?!

00:20:42.420 --> 00:20:45.590
Now, Pikachu!
100,000 Volts!

00:20:51.350 --> 00:20:53.940
<i>What an awful feeling!</i>

00:20:53.940 --> 00:20:56.400
<i>Sonansu!</i>

00:20:56.400 --> 00:20:57.980
All right!

00:20:59.900 --> 00:21:01.030
Huh? Again?

00:21:01.030 --> 00:21:01.990
Oh, no!

00:21:01.990 --> 00:21:02.780
It’s time!

00:21:03.280 --> 00:21:04.280
Time?

00:21:04.280 --> 00:21:07.990
There’s a launch event for a new
Marbled Candy in the next town!

00:21:07.990 --> 00:21:10.950
If I don’t hurry,
all the good seats will be gone!

00:21:10.950 --> 00:21:12.450
I must be off, too!

00:21:12.450 --> 00:21:14.710
Well, this is farewell, kids!

00:21:14.710 --> 00:21:17.580
Keep your nice Poké-Blue life going!

00:21:17.580 --> 00:21:18.710
Wait up!

00:21:19.540 --> 00:21:21.050
There they go.

00:21:21.840 --> 00:21:25.340
So, did they end up
becoming friends in the end?

00:21:25.340 --> 00:21:26.890
Who knows?

00:21:30.970 --> 00:21:35.190
Hobbies and ways of showing love
are as numerous as people and Pokémon...

00:21:35.770 --> 00:21:38.230
After spending time
with the Blue Pokémaniacs,

00:21:38.230 --> 00:21:43.490
Satoshi, Go, and Koharu’s horizons
have broadened a little.

00:23:07.190 --> 00:23:09.610
Now! Onto the next adventure!

00:23:09.610 --> 00:23:10.820
Go!

00:23:11.620 --> 00:23:14.330
All right! I get to battle Mr. Dande!

00:23:14.330 --> 00:23:16.410
It’s a tournament at Arabesque Gym!

00:23:16.410 --> 00:23:17.910
It must be unrelated
to the Championships.

00:23:17.910 --> 00:23:19.750
I’ll take whatever I can get!

00:23:19.750 --> 00:23:22.040
Anything’s good as long as
I get to battle Mr. Dande!

00:23:22.040 --> 00:23:25.960
But... Don’t you think
this stage smells sweet?

00:23:25.960 --> 00:23:27.210
Oh, now that you mention it...

00:23:27.210 --> 00:23:29.130
Something smells really good!

00:23:29.130 --> 00:23:31.050
Next time, on Pocket Monsters:

00:23:31.050 --> 00:23:33.720
Mawhip’s Sweet Battle?!
